# Stage 1: State Sync Implementation Plan

Implement the core infrastructure for state synchronization between the frontend UI and the AI context, allowing the AI to "see" what's on the user's screen.

## Proposed Changes

### Backend: AI Layer & Routing

#### [MODIFY] [main.py](file:///Users/oli/Desktop/CraftCanvas/backend/main.py)
Register the AI router which is currently defined but not active.
- Import `routers.ai` and include it in the FastAPI app with the prefix `/api/v1/ai`.

#### [NEW] [context_assembler.py](file:///Users/oli/Desktop/CraftCanvas/backend/services/context_assembler.py)
Create a dedicated service to handle prompt engineering and context merging.
- Implement `ContextAssembler` class.
- Add methods to format `UIContext` into a system prompt section.
- Merge DB-sourced academic data (from [context_providers.py](file:///Users/oli/Desktop/CraftCanvas/backend/services/context_providers.py)) with frontend `UIContext`.

#### [MODIFY] [ai.py](file:///Users/oli/Desktop/CraftCanvas/backend/routers/ai.py)
Update the API contract to handle state-aware chat.
- Add `ui_context` field to [ChatRequest](file:///Users/oli/Desktop/CraftCanvas/backend/routers/ai.py#21-24) pydantic model.
- Update `/chat` and `/chat/stream` (if applicable) to pass `ui_context` to the AI service.

#### [MODIFY] [ai_service.py](file:///Users/oli/Desktop/CraftCanvas/backend/services/ai_service.py)
- Refactor [chat](file:///Users/oli/Desktop/CraftCanvas/backend/routers/ai.py#26-42) method to accept `ui_context`.
- Update [_inject_context](file:///Users/oli/Desktop/CraftCanvas/backend/services/ai_service.py#30-86) to use `ContextAssembler`.

---

### Frontend: State Sync Infrastructure

#### [NEW] [uiContext.ts](file:///Users/oli/Desktop/CraftCanvas/frontend/lib/uiContext.ts)
Define the core data structures for state sync.
- `interface UIContext`: `activeView`, `visibleItems`, `filters`, `focusedItem`, `resolvedReferences`.
- `interface VisibleItem`: [id](file:///Users/oli/Desktop/CraftCanvas/backend/services/context_providers.py#89-107), `type`, `summary`.

#### [NEW] [UIContextProvider.tsx](file:///Users/oli/Desktop/CraftCanvas/frontend/lib/UIContextProvider.tsx)
Create the React Context engine for state sync.
- Implement `UIProvider` using `useReducer` to manage state.
- Provide hooks (`useUIContext`, `useUIDispatch`) for components to report visibility and read state.

#### [MODIFY] [layout.tsx](file:///Users/oli/Desktop/CraftCanvas/frontend/app/layout.tsx)
Wrap the application in `UIProvider` to enable global state awareness.

#### [MODIFY] [useChat.ts](file:///Users/oli/Desktop/CraftCanvas/frontend/hooks/useChat.ts)
- Use `useUIContext` to get the latest state snapshot.
- Include `uiContext` in the body of the POST request to `/api/v1/ai/chat`.

---

## Verification Plan

### Automated Tests
- Run existing tests to ensure no regressions:
  ```bash
  pytest backend/tests
  ```
- Create a new test `backend/tests/test_ai/test_context_assembler.py` to verify prompt formatting logic.

### Manual Verification
1. **Context Inspection**: Open the network tab in browser, send a chat message, and verify the `uiContext` field in the request payload contains correct `activeView` and matching `visibleItems`.
2. **AI Awareness Test**:
   - Navigate to the **Tasks** page.
   - Ask the AI: "Which tasks are currently visible on my screen?"
   - Verify that the AI lists the exact items shown in the task list.
3. **Navigation Sync**:
   - Move from **Tasks** to **Assignments**.
   - Send another message and verify the `activeView` in the request has changed.
